# CIFAR-10 Image Classifier (Flask + TensorFlow Lite)

A lightweight web app that classifies user-uploaded images into one of the 10 CIFAR-10
categories (airplane, automobile, bird, cat, deer, dog, frog, horse, ship, truck) using a
CNN trained in TensorFlow and served with TensorFlow Lite for fast, low-footprint inference.

## Features
- Simple browser UI (`index.html`) — upload an image, get a prediction + confidence score
- Flask backend (`appml.py`) serving a `.tflite` model
- Three exported model variants for comparing size/speed vs. accuracy trade-offs:
  - `cnn_baseline.tflite` — full-precision baseline
  - `cnn_quantized_float16.tflite` — float16 post-training quantization
  - `cnn_quantized_weights_only.tflite` — weights-only (int8) quantization

